-- title:
--   Generic points of the special fibre give minimal primes over (p)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Deligne–Rapoport package $\mathfrak{X}$ for the integral model `DRModel p`, i.e. the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\ \mathbb{Z}\ F\ j$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ built as the pushout of the two charts attached to the full modular function field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` and the element $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, together with all the data recorded in the structure `DRModelPackage` (properness, flatness, integrality and normality of `DRModel.toBase p`, the rational and geometric curve models with their identifications, the cusp sections, the smooth locus, and the further fields of the structure). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin ℤ F j`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$, and $\iota =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin` for the corresponding chart morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `DRModel p`. Consider the two points of the base change of `DRModel p` to $O$ obtained by applying, to the generic point of the scheme underlying the curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\ \kappa$, first $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\ \kappa$ (respectively $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\ \kappa$) followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, and then the first pullback projection. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions, one for each of these two points: for every prime $P$ of $A$, if $\iota$ sends $P$ to that point, then the ideal $P$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $A$ generated by $p$.
--
--   The statement locates the images in the finite chart of the two generic points of the characteristic-$p$ fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model: they are, on the chart $\operatorname{Spec} A$, exactly generic points of components of the fibre over $(p)$. It is used in the analysis of stalks and function values on the model, being cited by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.polynomialEval_mem_range_algebraMap_stalk_and_inv_mem_of_map_ne_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.polynomialEval_mem_range_algebraMap_stalk_and_inv_mem_of_map_ne_zero).
